---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';
import { getPracticeURL, withPracticeURL } from '../../lib/practice';
import testFailure from '../../samples/vitest-failure.txt?raw';
import vitestExample from '../../samples/vitest-example.ts.txt?raw';

const practiceURL = getPracticeURL(Astro);
const scopedSample = [
   `import { describe } from 'vitest';`,
   `import { test } from 'a11ied/vitest';`,
   '',
   `describe('checkout', () => {`,
   `   test.scoped({ srOptions: { url: 'http://localhost:3000/checkout' } });`,
   '',
   `   test('has one main heading', ({ sr }) => {`,
   `      sr.next('heading').expect.spoken('heading, Checkout, level 1');`,
   '   });',
   '});',
].join('\n');
const configSample = [
   `import { playwright } from '@vitest/browser-playwright';`,
   `import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';`,
   '',
   'export default defineConfig({',
   '   test: {',
   '      browser: {',
   '         enabled: true,',
   '         provider: playwright(),',
   `         instances: [{ browser: 'chromium' }],`,
   '      },',
   '   },',
   '});',
].join('\n');
const browserSample = [
   `import { test } from 'a11ied/browser';`,
   `import { render } from 'vitest-browser-react';`,
   `import { PayButton } from './pay-button';`,
   '',
   `test('announces the price', ({ sr }) => {`,
   '   render(<PayButton amount="12.00" />);',
   '',
   `   sr.next('button');`,
   `   sr.expectCursorOn({ role: 'button', name: 'Pay 12.00' });`,
   '});',
].join('\n');
const toc = [
   { id: 'install', label: 'Install' },
   { id: 'example', label: 'A first test file' },
   { id: 'fixture', label: 'The sr fixture' },
   { id: 'queue', label: 'Commands run in order' },
   { id: 'fail', label: 'When a check fails' },
   { id: 'timeouts', label: 'Timeouts' },
   { id: 'matchers', label: 'Matchers' },
   { id: 'browser', label: 'Vitest browser mode' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="Test with Vitest"
   summary="<p><code>a11ied/vitest</code> gives every test a screen reader named <code>sr</code>. Call its methods one after another, with no <code>await</code>, and the test fails when an announcement is missing. It needs Vitest 4 or later.</p>"
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section>
      <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
      <pre><code>npm install --save-dev a11ied vitest</code></pre>
      <p>
         Tests that open a URL need Chrome, Edge, Brave, or Chromium on the machine.
         <code>npx playwright install chromium</code> adds one.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="example">A first test file</h2>
      <p>
         These tests run against the docs' <a href="/guides/demo">practice page</a>, a demo
         page with a working copy and a broken copy. They use the working copy. Copy the file
         and run <code>npx vitest</code>.
      </p>
      <pre data-label="invite.test.ts"><code>{withPracticeURL(vitestExample, practiceURL)}</code></pre>
      <p>The three tests show the three ways to write one.</p>
      <ol>
         <li>A chain. Each call returns an object with every method on it. <code>expect</code> starts a check and <code>and</code> adds another.</li>
         <li>One statement per step. The result is the same.</li>
         <li>An <code>await</code>, for the one time a test needs a value back.</li>
      </ol>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="fixture">The sr fixture</h2>
      <p>
         Import <code>test</code> from <code>a11ied/vitest</code> in place of Vitest's own. It
         starts a screen reader before each test and stops it after, whether the test passed
         or failed. <code>srOptions</code> says what to read. Set it for a file with
         <code>test.extend</code>, as in the first test file, or for a block with <code>test.scoped</code>.
      </p>
      <pre data-label="checkout.test.ts"><code>{scopedSample}</code></pre>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>url</code> or <code>html</code></dt>
         <dd>The page to read. Inline <code>html</code> runs in jsdom, where page scripts do not run.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr</code></dt>
         <dd><code>'virtual'</code> by default, or <code>'voiceover'</code> or <code>'nvda'</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>timeoutMs</code></dt>
         <dd>A limit for each command.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         Each test gets its own reader inside the test process, so tests in parallel workers
         do not interfere. The other options are in the
         <a href="/reference/api#test">API reference</a>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="queue">Commands run in order</h2>
      <p>
         A call to <code>sr</code> queues a command and returns at once. The commands run one
         at a time, in the order you wrote them. After your test function returns, Vitest
         waits for the queue, so you write no <code>await</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
         Await a call when you need what it returns. The <code>await</code> runs everything
         queued before it, then that call.
      </p>
      <pre data-label="TypeScript"><code>{`const item = await sr.read();`}</code></pre>
      <p>
         The methods are the ones in
         <a href="/guides/testing#methods">write screen reader tests</a>. In a chain, the
         checks are named <code>spoken</code>, <code>spokenInOrder</code>, and
         <code>cursorOn</code>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="fail">When a check fails</h2>
      <p>
         Point the first test at the broken copy of the practice page, where the dialog never takes
         focus. Vitest reports the line and what the screen reader said.
      </p>
      <pre data-label="OUTPUT"><code>{testFailure.trimEnd()}</code></pre>
      <p>
         When a command fails, the commands queued after it are skipped. To test that
         something is <em>not</em> announced, use <code>not</code>:
      </p>
      <pre data-label="TypeScript"><code>{`sr.expectSpoken(/error/iu, { not: true });`}</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="timeouts">Timeouts</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>A check</dt>
         <dd>Checks again every 100 ms for up to 5000 ms, so a late announcement still counts. Set <code>timeoutMs</code> on the check to change it, or <code>0</code> to check once.</dd>
         <dt>A test</dt>
         <dd>Queued commands run inside Vitest's <code>testTimeout</code>, 5000 ms by default. Raise it for a long sequence: pass a third argument to the test, or set it in <code>vitest.config.ts</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="matchers">Matchers</h2>
      <p>
         Importing <code>a11ied/vitest</code> also adds three matchers to Vitest's
         <code>expect</code>, for when you prefer that style.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs defs--wide">
         <dt><code>toHaveSpoken(match)</code></dt>
         <dd>An announcement matches.</dd>
         <dt><code>toHaveSpokenInOrder([a, b, c])</code></dt>
         <dd>Each match comes after the one before it.</dd>
         <dt><code>toHaveCursorOn(&#123; role, name &#125;)</code></dt>
         <dd>The element under the cursor matches.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre data-label="TypeScript"><code>{`await expect(sr).toHaveSpoken('dialog, Invite member');\nawait expect.poll(() => sr.transcript()).toHaveSpoken('Invitation sent');`}</code></pre>
      <p>
         A matcher checks once and does not wait. Wrap it in <code>expect.poll</code> for an
         announcement that arrives later, or use the <code>sr.expectSpoken</code> family,
         which waits.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="browser">Vitest browser mode</h2>
      <p>
         In browser mode the test already runs in a browser.
         <code>a11ied/browser</code> starts the simulated screen reader on that page, so you
         mount a component and read it. There is no URL and no second page load.
      </p>
      <pre data-label="vitest.config.ts"><code>{configSample}</code></pre>
      <pre data-label="pay-button.browser.test.tsx"><code>{browserSample}</code></pre>
      <p>
         The <code>sr</code> fixture reads the whole document body. To read one mounted
         component, start your own reader with
         <code>queuedScreenReader(&#123; container &#125;)</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
         Two methods throw in browser mode: <code>open()</code>, because the page is the
         test's own, and <code>perform()</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
         A container with no role of its own has no top or bottom for the screen reader to
         find. <code>top()</code> and <code>bottom()</code> then fail with
         <code>virtual-tree-edge-unavailable</code>. Use <code>readAll()</code> in its place.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
